From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] core: kept-state walks gated by the last id (TF_GLM_OVN_KEPT_WALK)

ai-engine e9bc5dc54 grafted onto the pin. Every kept-state walk (keptNear,
wouldServe, reserve, forget, keepBorn, find, interior, imprint, disk matches,
extendedScan, link) checks the last id first and compares with one vectorised
helper (prompt_prefix.same): prompt_prefix.zig with starts/ends/Lazy, the count
and property tests, the bench. Same decisions, entries and links: the pin's
images.matches and own_only conditions stay in their walks, the test-ref block
moved from prompt_cache.zig (at the 600-line limit) to engine_api_test.zig, the
cascade root that already references prompt_cache.zig.

Measurement (ai-engine docs/PARITY.md item, e9bc5dc54): laptop warm turn at
600k, 32 kept states, 540 -> 3.0 ms; 29 mutants killed. Behaviour-identical
by construction (property test over 24 random sessions; count test per walk).

Gates on pin+0001..0006: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host
green (550 tests, 1 skipped), whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new.

Folded in by the 2026-11-12 fold (work/fold/MAP.tsv), each hunk where it belongs:
- 0041: keepBorn is 'the same state again' only at the same length

Re-seated on v1.2.7 (93a2e93ecebff8aa52b88e58c5dd222516e69c5f, from pin 9c9bf542) by the 2026-11-12 re-seat (work/reseat/DECISIONS.md):
- lean_check.py's HIDDEN_GETENV: prompt_prefix.gated() read platform.c.getenv(knob); TF_GLM_OVN_KEPT_WALK is now a .glm flag row read by environment.read (0 or 1; the old reader took any text but empty and 0 as on), and the parser's test checks the row instead.
- fold-series.md F8 is wrong: KEPT_WALK is a real switch (prompt_prefix.gated()), off by default; every walk with it off asks exactly as before (Lazy compares at once, beyond() is true, starts() is std.mem.eql).
- Upstream moved keepBorn to prompt_cache_keep.zig and Store.reserve to prompt_cache_reserve.zig (exists()): their compares take prefix.starts there; the rest of the walks are where the pin had them.
- v1.2.7's Entry already has `seen` (prompt_cache_status.Seen, the dashboard's times): the link walk's mark is renamed Entry.proved.
- v1.2.7's link() also links equal-born entries (a request's reply end): prove() now marks every entry born no later than the new one (o.born > x.born skips), or the gated link would drop those links; victimIn and extendedScan keep v1.2.7's born rule (born == e.born and !e.rewind) and its reservation_guard skip.
- prompt_cache.zig is 525 lines at v1.2.7, not 600: its test block stays where upstream has it and engine_api_test.zig is not touched (the fold moved the block only for the 600-line rule).
- Not converted, upstream walks the fold never saw: lookupUserAt's rewind tag, prompt_cache_divergence.report, reserve's Guard.protects and reclaimable, policy.redundant/own/continuedLater, prompt_cache_lifetime.
- source: work/fold/0009-kept-walk-prefix-helper.patch

